  "id": "COMPOUND:14388 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that fenofibrate may interact with CCRF-HSB-2 through multiple indirect pathways. The highest-scoring pathway links fenofibrate to CCRF-HSB-2 via the compound 6-[(1R,5S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-4-methylcyclohex-2-en-1-yl]-2-methylhept-2-en-4-one, which is itself a target of CCRF-HSB-2. This indicates a potential mechanism where fenofibrate may modulate the activity of this compound, which in turn affects CCRF-HSB-2. Another pathway connects fenofibrate to DNA polymerase iota, which is targeted by Sibiriquinone B, and this enzyme is also targeted by (3S)-3-Hydroxybutanoic Acid, all of which ultimately target CCRF-HSB-2. These findings suggest that fenofibrate may exert its effects through a network of molecular interactions that ultimately influence CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence is consistent with a role for fenofibrate in modulating the activity of downstream targets, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
